oa-hoa-vs-poa/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-4x3.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/hoa-hoa-vs-poa/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-4x3.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","description":"Tall oceanfront towers along the beach in Myrtle Beach, with a row of more towers into the distance","creator":{"@type":"Person","name":"DiscoA340"},"creditText":"DiscoA340, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons","copyrightNotice":"© DiscoA340, CC BY-SA 4.0","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","acquireLicensePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hotels_along_the_Grand_Strand_Beachfront_2.jpg","isBasedOn":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hotels_along_the_Grand_Strand_Beachfront_2.jpg"},{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/hoa-hoa-vs-poa/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-16x9.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/hoa-hoa-vs-poa/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-16x9.webp","width":1200,"height":675,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","description":"Tall oceanfront towers along the beach in Myrtle Beach, with a row of more towers into the distance","creator":{"@type":"Person","name":"DiscoA340"},"creditText":"DiscoA340, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons","copyrightNotice":"© DiscoA340, CC BY-SA 4.0","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","acquireLicensePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hotels_along_the_Grand_Strand_Beachfront_2.jpg","isBasedOn":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hotels_along_the_Grand_Strand_Beachfront_2.jpg"}],"mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/hoa/hoa-vs-poa/"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"Homeowners associations, property owners associations and condo regimes (horizontal property regimes) in South Carolina"},"keywords":"HOA vs POA, HOA vs POA South Carolina, is a POA the same as an HOA, property owners association South Carolina, regime fee South Carolina, horizontal property regime, condo association vs HOA, master association vs HOA, two HOA fees, HOA fees Myrtle Beach, Horizontal Property Act South Carolina"}</script>
+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is an HOA the same as a POA in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, in law. South Carolina's HOA Act counts as a homeowners association any group that runs a planned neighborhood or a condo regime under a recorded declaration that makes owners pay, except a timeshare plan. A property owners association that meets that test is one too."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a regime fee in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A regime fee is the condo fee. South Carolina's law calls a condo a horizontal property regime, so the fee its owners pay is called a regime fee. The typical condo fee for sale on the Grand Strand is about $640 a month."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What do I own in a condo?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Your unit alone, plus a share of the common parts, given as a percentage in the condo's founding document. The common parts stay undivided; no owner can force them to be split up, and selling a unit sells its share with it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who insures a condo building in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The association. South Carolina's condo law makes the owners' association insure the property, and each owner may also insure their own unit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much are HOA fees on the Grand Strand?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For homes for sale, the typical monthly fee is about $640 for a condo, $275 for a townhouse and $95 for a house. About three in ten houses for sale have no association at all."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a home have two HOAs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. In a master-planned community, a home can belong to a master association and to a neighborhood association or condo regime inside it, each with its own documents. Grande Dunes, Barefoot Resort and Prince Creek all have more than one layer in the county record."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a POA voluntary in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A POA is voluntary only when no recorded document makes owners pay, and then it is not an HOA under South Carolina's HOA Act. The letters POA in the name do not change that."}}]}</script>
