+D. Cancellation of the Policy by Us
+
+A. Policy Nullification for Fraud,
+Misrepresentation, or Making False Statements
+1. With respect to all insureds under this
+policy, this policy is void and has no legal
+force and effect if at any time, before or
+after a loss, you or any other insured or your
+agent have, with respect to this policy or
+any other NFIP insurance:
+a. Concealed or misrepresented any material fact or circumstance;
+b. Engaged in fraudulent conduct; or
+c. Made false statements.
+2. Policies voided under A.1 cannot be renewed or replaced by a new NFIP policy.
+3. Policies are void as of the date the acts
+described in A.1.above were committed.
+4. Fines, civil penalties, and imprisonment
+under applicable Federal laws may also
+apply to the acts of fraud or concealment described above.
